{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4337162","formula":"AcPO₄","hill":"AcO4P","elements":["O","P","Ac"],"composition":{"O":4.0,"P":1.0,"Ac":1.0},"names":{"en":"Actinium(III) orthophosphate","ru":"Ортофосфат актиния(III)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Actinium(III) phosphate is a white-colored chemical compound of the radioactive element actinium. This salt was created by reacting actinium(III) chloride with monosodium phosphate in aqueous hydrochloric acid. This resulted in the hemihydrate AcPO4·1/2H2O, whose structure was confirmed by x-ray diffraction to match that of lanthanum phosphate.","ru":"Ортофосфат актиния(III) (фосфорнокислый актиний) — AcPO4, неорганическое соединение, актиниевая соль ортофосфорной кислоты. В свободном виде достоверно не получен, существует в форме кристаллогидрата: AcPO4 • 0,5H2O. Белое вещество, малорастворимое в воде."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4337162","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Actinium%28III%29_phosphate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9E%D1%80%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%84%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%84%D0%B0%D1%82_%D0%B0%D0%BA%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%8F%28III%29","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q109347834","formula":"O₄PPm","names":{"en":"Promethium phosphate"},"elements":["O","P","Pm"],"fame":6,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q4946255","formula":"BN₃O₉","names":{"en":"Boron nitrate"},"elements":["B","N","O"],"fame":9,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q18358153","formula":"N₃O₁₀V","names":{"en":"Vanadyl nitrate"},"elements":["N","O","V"],"fame":6,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q415471","for